Prefer `task.enrolled()` over the finding's first suggestion `len(seeds)`. The two are numerically identical at :1481 (the enqueue loop has just run and, in step 4, nothing else ever enrols), but `task.enrolled()` is better on three counts:
 - it makes the opening line and its closing partner at :1499-1500 report the same quantity, so "starting ... with N entries" and "agent finished, k/N interpreted" line up instead of contradicting each other;
 - it is derived from `state`, which is the discipline §15.8 fixes for these counts ("The counters of §12 #13-#16 are derived from `state`, never from `results`"), and it is exactly §12's N (`count(state != _NOT_ENROLLED)`);
